flowchart TD
    A[Need a collection] --> C{Access pattern?}
    C -- Single-threaded only --> B{Key-value pairs?}
    C -- Externally synchronised<br/>(e.g. wrapper) --> B
    C -- Concurrent access --> D{Concurrent needs?}

    %% ── Non-concurrent: key-value ──
    B -- Yes --> E{Key type is enum?}
    E -- Yes --> F[EnumMap<br/>Array-backed high performance<br/>for enum keys]
    E -- No --> G{Insertion order or sorted keys?}
    G -- Yes, insertion order --> H[LinkedHashMap]
    G -- Yes, sorted keys --> I[TreeMap]
    G -- No --> J[HashMap<br/>Allows null keys and values]
    B -- Immutable snapshot needed --> K[List.of / Set.of / Map.of<br/>Null-rejecting and unmodifiable<br/>small-collection optimisation]

    %% ── Non-concurrent: no key-value ──
    B -- No --> L{Duplicates allowed?}
    L -- No --> M{Need sorted order?}
    M -- Yes --> N[TreeSet]
    M -- No, need insertion order --> O[LinkedHashSet]
    M -- No --> P[HashSet]
    L -- Yes --> Q{Frequent index access?}
    Q -- Yes --> R[ArrayList]
    Q -- No, frequent insert/remove at<br/>ends, double-ended queue needed --> S[ArrayDeque<br/>Implements Deque, rejects null elements]
    Q -- No, frequent insert/remove in<br/>middle --> T[LinkedList<br/>Higher per-element memory overhead<br/>than ArrayList]
    L -- Yes, ordering without sorting,<br/>no indexed access needed --> U[PriorityQueue<br/>Heap-ordered, no stable sorting<br/>no indexed access]

    %% ── Concurrent: key-value ──
    D -- Key-value pairs --> V[ConcurrentHashMap<br/>Segmented locking, weakly consistent<br/>iterators, rejects null keys and values]

    %% ── Concurrent: queue / blocking ──
    D -- Queue, blocking<br/>producer/consumer --> W{Producer/consumer<br/>blocking needed?}
    W -- Yes, blocking queue --> X[BlockingQueue subtypes:<br/>ArrayBlockingQueue - bounded / array<br/>LinkedBlockingQueue - optional bound / linked<br/>PriorityBlockingQueue - unbounded / heap<br/>DelayQueue - delayed elements<br/>SynchronousQueue - handoff / no capacity]
    W -- No, lock-free FIFO --> Y[ConcurrentLinkedQueue<br/>Lock-free, non-blocking FIFO<br/>Rejects null elements]

    %% ── Concurrent: list, read-heavy ──
    D -- List, read-heavy<br/>write-rare --> Z[CopyOnWriteArrayList<br/>Snapshot iterators, high read / low write<br/>Memory cost on mutation]

    %% ── Defensive-copy note ──
    A -.->|Defensive copies, unmodifiable<br/>wrappers, immutable factories avoid<br/>accidental mutation of shared references| GA[Defensive copy /<br/>unmodifiable wrapper /<br/>immutable factory]
